Taints are set on nodes , Tolerations are set on pod
k taint node node-name key=value:taint-effect
NoSchedule - pods will not schedule on the nodes. Existing pod with not evict 
PreferNoSchedule - s/w will try to avoid placing a pod on the node but not guaranteed
NoExecute - new pods will not be scheduled on the nodes & existing ones on the nodes if any will be evicted if they dont tolerate the taint
Taints & Tolerations doesn't tell the pod to goto a particular node infact it tells the node to accept pods with certain toleration. If we want to restrict pod to particular nodes then we will use node affinity
A taint is  setup on Mater node as NoSchedule to avoid scheduling of applications on master node



